This is a project that aims to remove the complexity(LOL) from buying a dashcam. The market is flooded with offerings at all price points and walled garden ecosystems that were at least for me, confusing to navigate.

So here we are, the goal of this project is to make an open source Dashcam solution using a raspberry pi and off the shelf webcams in an interface that just works. 

I've tried to make it as easy as possible to build this project from source, you can test it on your local machine, but it is advised that you build the project directly on your raspberry pi.

1. clone the repository
2. run the init-system.sh script. Feel free to audit this, its primary purpose is to install all the dependencies that this project requires. The major one being VCPKG, which also gets configured.
3. That's it. The script will also build the project at the end and store it in 
    {project_root}/build/debug
    And you can execute it by running ./{project_root}/build/debug/src/Dashcam

If you run into any issues please report it at
    https://github.com/Endon55/Dashcam/issues

Or if you have ideas to improve the software feel free to leave them as well.
